  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Central Nexus model registry. A model entry is vendor-neutral configuration: it maps a profile-facing model id to a provider configuration identifier (settings.yaml llm-pi-ai.providers) and declares capabilities. Routing/controller code must never branch on vendor; vendor-specific handling belongs only in provider adapters and enforcement layers. Optional `agentEngines` (Phase M2) scopes an entry to agent engines: entries WITHOUT the property serve the Dual role architecture exactly as before; a declaration that omits 'dual' (e.g. [\"muse\"]) excludes the entry from every Dual role list. Optional `dataUseTier` (Phase M2) preserves the standard/contributor checkpoint distinction for later outbound-sanitization logic; it must never be inferred from the model-name string. `maxOutputTokens` (Phase M2.1) is a VENDOR-VERIFIED hard output ceiling taken from official vendor documentation and is never a Nexus safety/default cap: when no official ceiling is published the field must be omitted rather than guessed, and Nexus operational/request-level caps live at the call sites that impose them (never in this registry).",
